A||N||8||Taijiguy||On the topic of speakers.....||||1||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||03-22-2001||08:38 PM||||I think I know the answer already before I ask this question, but I'll ask it anyway. I'm wanting to bring up the quality of the sound in my GT. Due to the extent of the mods I've done, I have the entire ECM enclosure area in which to mount some subs. (The ECM has magically disappeared) I'm trying to decided between a single 8" sub or two 6" subs. I'm not looking for panel rattling bass, I'm looking for nice, accurate sound at slightly elevated sound pressure levels. I'll leave the ear-bleeding to the backwards-hat boys. I'm running two 150 watt amps, one powering the Kicker 4x10's in the dash, the other waiting for the subs. Active crossover, all that hoorah. Might be convinced to install a cap if it'll help any. This is a budget project. My initital response is the 2 6's, but I'm looking for other suggestions. The floor is now officially open for discussion!<BR>TIA<BR>Taiji<BR>-Do not meddle in the affairs of wizards<BR>-For you are crunchy and good with ketchup||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-22-2001||08:45 PM||||You will get better low frequency reproduction with one 8" sub as opposed to twin 6.5's. Also the distortion level will be less. I would go with a single 8" (OOOPS, I am going with a single 8" in my set-up that I am building now) A quality 8" will also be more efficent use of power than a pair of 6.5's. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-24-2001||12:12 PM||||Where did you put the ECM??  I wouldn't mind moving mine out of the way.||||reg||1
